---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About The Margin of Error and Hans W. A. Hanley.">
	<section class="standard-page about-page">
		<header class="page-heading">
			<p class="kicker">Colophon</p>
			<h1>About the margin</h1>
		</header>
		<div class="about-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<p class="standfirst">
					The Margin of Error is an independent publication about computer science,
					disinformation, statistics, and world events.
				</p>
				<p>
					It is written by <a href="https://www.hanshanley.com/">Hans W. A. Hanley</a>.
					Some pieces are arguments. Others begin with a dataset, a network, or a question
					that needs to be computed before it can be discussed.
				</p>
				<p>
					When a piece has supporting code, data, outputs, or an interactive instrument,
					those materials live beside the article. When it does not, the writing stands on
					its own—no empty dashboards and no decorative machinery.
				</p>
			</div>
			<aside class="about-aside">
				<p class="kicker">Elsewhere</p>
				<a href="https://www.hanshanley.com/">Academic work</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/hanshanley">GitHub</a>
				<a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeHPhVHdJ0xdCYq3wDYjkOIxgVdErP4qszNOBQYrnyzTz3xyQ/viewform">Subscribe</a>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
